  "pipeline_reference": "~2e9 kernel evaluations for the whole Moon (~118,000 tiles x ~38 candidates x ~500 support vectors; pipeline section 'Quantum kernel development and validation')",
  "note": "one kernel evaluation = one compute-uncompute circuit (QK-A, QK-Z) or, for QK-P, one of the 3 measurement circuits of a sample (largest reported); transpiled once with the angles as parameters (the counts do not depend on the angles: R_Z is virtual); duration = longest path with the gate and readout durations of the calibration; physical_s = shots x (duration + rep_delay), execution only at the default rep_delay; clops_s = circuits x shots x max(1, two-qubit layers) / CLOPS_h, an approximation (CLOPS_h is measured on full-width layers); times scale linearly with the shots per circuit; extrapolation: candidates = owned sub-tiles of R x stage-1 candidate share (QH3), whole Moon by the ratio of the areas (latitude-dependent crater density and polar coverage ignored)"
 }
